{"title":"Career Roadmap · Diagnostic Centre Manager","role":"Diagnostic Centre Manager","summary":"A Diagnostic Centre Manager manages the operational, technical-support, quality, administrative, and customer-service functions of a diagnostic laboratory or diagnostic centre.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Medical Laboratory Technology (BMLT / B.Sc MLT)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Diagnostic Centre Manager manages the operational, technical-support, quality, administrative, and customer-service functions of a diagnostic laboratory or diagnostic centre."},{"type":"p","text":"For a BMLT / B.Sc MLT graduate, the ideal pathway combines medical laboratory science + quality management + laboratory operations + people management + healthcare administration."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Laboratory workflow management"},{"text":"Sample collection and processing coordination"},{"text":"Staff scheduling"},{"text":"Inventory management"},{"text":"Quality assurance"},{"text":"Equipment coordination"},{"text":"Turnaround-time monitoring"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Patient-service management"},{"text":"Regulatory and accreditation readiness"},{"text":"Vendor management"},{"text":"Cost and resource management"},{"text":"Coordination with pathologists, laboratory professionals and clinicians"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The manager may not personally perform every technical laboratory procedure; the role increasingly focuses on safe, efficient, compliant and financially sustainable laboratory operations."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BMLT / B.Sc MLT","Clinical Laboratory Internship","Medical Laboratory Technologist","Senior Laboratory Technologist","Section / Shift In-Charge","Laboratory Supervisor